{"name":"Sister Loganberry Frost","hex":"#863f76","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sister","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A daughter of the same parents as another person; a female sibling.","A female member of a religious order; especially one devoted to more active service;  a nun."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strengthen (a supporting beam) by fastening a second beam alongside it.","To be sister to; to resemble closely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sister"},{"term":"loganberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hybrid berry, produced by crossing a raspberry with a blackberry, considered a species Rubus loganobaccus, a variety Rubus ursinus var. loganobaccus, or a nothospecies Rubus × loganobaccus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loganberry"},{"term":"frost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cover of minute ice crystals on objects that are exposed to the air. Frost is formed by the same process as dew, except that the temperature of the frosted object is below freezing.","The cold weather that causes these ice crystals to form."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with frost.","To become covered with frost."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sister","blocks":[{"text":"A sister is a woman or a girl who shares parents or a parent with another individual; a female sibling. The male counterpart is a brother. Although the term typically refers to a familial relationship, it is sometimes used endearingly to refer to non-familial relationships. A full sister is a first-degree relative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Little_Julia_tending_the_baby_at_home.jpg/330px-Little_Julia_tending_the_baby_at_home.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sister"},{"title":"Loganberry","blocks":[{"text":"The loganberry is a hybrid of the North American blackberry and the European raspberry, accidentally bred in 1881 by James Harvey Logan, for whom they are named. It is cultivated for its edible fruit."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/Rubus_loganobaccus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loganberry"},{"title":"Frost","blocks":[{"text":"Frost is a layer of ice on a solid surface, which forms from water vapor that deposits onto a freezing surface. Frost forms when the air contains more water vapor than it can normally hold at a specific temperature. The process is similar to the formation of dew, except it occurs below the freezing point of water typically without crossing through a liquid state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg/330px-Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frost"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/The_Chess_Game_%28Sofonisba_Anguissola%29_1555_%284096x3236px%29.jpg/500px-The_Chess_Game_%28Sofonisba_Anguissola%29_1555_%284096x3236px%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/The_Chess_Game_%28Sofonisba_Anguissola%29_1555_%284096x3236px%29.jpg/1280px-The_Chess_Game_%28Sofonisba_Anguissola%29_1555_%284096x3236px%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/The_Chess_Game_%28Sofonisba_Anguissola%29_1555_%284096x3236px%29.jpg/500px-The_Chess_Game_%28Sofonisba_Anguissola%29_1555_%284096x3236px%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Game of Chess (1555) by Sofonisba Anguissola (It depicts